From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:22:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 082/110] Clone to other view works for unsaved and untitled
 tabs

Like Notepad++, any editor tab can be cloned: the clone starts with the
current text, unsaved edits included, and the same changed state, and is
paired at once so edits mirror both ways. Clones are paired by a link
rather than by path, so untitled tabs pair too; tabs of one file without a
link still pair by path. Save As in one clone gives every clone the new
path, and the session keeps the link, so restored unsaved or untitled
clones come back paired.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

